# Who fixes what

Before writing code, read `docs/design/who-fixes-what.md`.

Alfred owns application logic, the database, infrastructure, and any product decision still open, and he merges those pull requests. Item 1 is draft #86. Open work awaiting him, not on that ordered list: drafts #89, #91, and #137; ready for review #128, #133, #134, #136, #138, and #139. #127 merged on 23 Oct 2026. It changed `quant/trade/order_policy.py`, `quant/trade/models/order.py`, docs, and tests. Application code. Alfred merged it. Bots do not own it. #128 is ready for review. #127 has merged, so #128 needs its branch brought up to date with main before review. That is Alfred's pull request. Do not touch its branch. Still application code. Alfred merges it. #137 follows #128. Do not merge #137 before #128. After #128 merges, rebase #137 onto main. It stays a draft until then. Application code. Alfred merges it. #134 changes a Liquibase refdata release comment and tests. Alfred merges it. Bots do not own it. #136 changes `quant/trade/brokers/ccxt/confirm.py` and `tests/unit/test_ccxt_confirm.py`. Application code. Alfred merges it. #138 changes only `tests/unit/test_order_policy.py` and `tests/unit/test_refdata_reader.py`. Test-only. A test-only pull request still goes to Alfred. #139 changes `scripts/appctl.sh` and `docs/architecture/dev-vs-prod.md`. Infrastructure. Alfred merges it. #126 merged on 22 Oct 2026. Alfred merged it. Bots do not own it. #129 merged on 22 Oct 2026. Alfred merged it. Bots do not own it. #124 merged on 22 Oct 2026. It changed only `scripts/bybit_local_testnet.py` and `tests/unit/test_bybit_local_testnet.py`. It is an offline harness that does not change live behaviour. Alfred merged it. #125 merged on 22 Oct 2026. It changed `quant/trade/brokers/ccxt/confirm.py` and tests. Alfred merged it. Bots do not own it. #132 merged on 22 Oct 2026. Alfred merged it. It is a docs change.

Bots own a verified small bug, docs, research notes, and an offline harness that does not change live behaviour. Open #135 changes `scripts/bybit_local_testnet.py`, `tests/unit/test_bybit_local_testnet.py`, `tests/integration/test_ccxt_dry_run.py`, and adds `tests/unit/test_ccxt_dry_run_fixture.py`. Every file is on `deploy.yml` `paths-ignore`, so a bot may merge it once review has passed and CI is green. It is ready for review. A test-only pull request still goes to Alfred.

A pull request stays a draft until review has passed, CI is green, and nothing is waiting on a decision. Bots never self-merge an application-code pull request (`quant/**`, frontend, Liquibase, infra). Docs must not recommend risk numbers. Every code change reuses or extends existing utilities, classes, readers, and fields. A review fails a pull request that duplicates an existing object. The rule is `docs/design/coding-standards.md`.

- If the task is on Alfred's list, do not implement it.
- If it is an open product decision, stop and say so.
- If it is on the bot list and is a verified bug under about 20 lines of real code, it can be a small fix.
- Do not push to or change the draft state of a pull request a person opened rather than a bot. Alfred reviews and merges it.
